# A remove hit moves the value out of the entry it removes to its result, with no copy and release, and ends the table's key count; scalar parts need none, and constant keys still clean up the stored key.
fn remove_value[V](values: &mut Map[string, V], key: string) -> V?:
    values.remove(key)
